; A constructor's shape word must not depend on whether the
; constructor ran inside a lambda.
;
; Three emitters read the same per-field evidence witness out of a
; call's stamp. `emitPrimRetainRef` enumerated THREE witness classes -
; unconditional, "bit k of the enclosing function's evidence word",
; and `EV_LAMARG - d`, the lifted lambda's own argument, whose class
; only the application knows. The two CONSTRUCTOR emitters enumerated
; two and let the third fall into a silent else: `fieldRetainCode`
; answered -1 ("no retain") and `ctorShapeEmit` set no map bit.
;
; So until 2026-09-03 the same value at the same type got two
; different headers:
;
;     (fn (wrap x) (Some x))                    131076  bitmap 0b10
;     (fn (viaLam s) ((lambda (x) (Some x)) s))      4  LEAF
;
; The lambda-built block claimed to hold no references, so the walk at
; its death never handed the payload's share back. It did not crash:
; the two halves were wrong TOGETHER - the store took no share and the
; map promised none - which is why every gate stayed green. It was a
; leak, and the pair is why fixing one half alone would have been
; worse than the bug: a map bit without its store is an OVER-release.
;
; Both halves therefore land together, and terms 2 and 5 are what say
; so.
;
; The shape word is `padded-word-count * 2` plus a bit `17 + j` per
; reference field j, so 131076 is "4 payload words, field 0 is a
; reference" and 393224 is "4 words, fields 0 and 1 are references".
;
; What each term establishes:
;
;   1. THE DEFECT. `(Some s)` built outside a lambda and inside one
;      report the SAME shape word. Two numbers, not one: a regression
;      shows up as a difference between two lines rather than as one
;      line moving.
;   2. THE STORE TOOK THE SHARE. The payload String's own count under
;      each. This is the half that makes term 1 safe - a shape bit
;      whose store never retained is an over-release, and this is the
;      line that would catch it. Both must read 2: the local binding's
;      share and the field's.
;   3. TWO reference fields, and the two witness classes side by side:
;      field 0 is the lambda's own argument, field 1 is a capture of
;      the enclosing function's parameter, which always worked. The
;      broken half is exactly the bit the plain build has and this one
;      lost.
;   4. TWO LAMBDAS DEEP, so both fields are lambda arguments at
;      DIFFERENT depths - `y` at depth 0 and `x` one level out, caught
;      by `evwaSym`'s level shift. A fix that read only depth 0 passes
;      term 3 and fails here.
;   5. THE OVER-RELEASE CONTROL, and the reason the bit has to be
;      emitted as a run-time read rather than folded into the
;      constant. The SAME lifted lambda serves `(Option Int)` and
;      `(Option String)`; only the application knows which. An `Int`
;      payload must still read LEAF. A fix that set the bit
;      unconditionally would make this line 131076 and would be
;      handing back a share the store never took.
(import IO)

(import Str)

(data Two (a b) (Mk a b))

; the shape word sits one word above the count, at `p - 8`
(:: shapeOf (-> Int Int))

(fn (shapeOf p) (__load64 (- p 16) 1))

(:: payloadRc (-> Int Int))

(fn (payloadRc p) (__load64 (- (__load64 p 1) 16) 0))

(:: fieldRc (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (fieldRc p j) (__load64 (- (__load64 p j) 16) 0))

; --- 1, 2: the same value at the same type, two ways ---
(:: wrap (-> a (Option a)))

(fn (wrap x) (Some x))

(:: viaLam (-> String (Option String)))

(fn (viaLam s) ((lambda (x) (Some x)) s))

; --- 3: two reference fields, built outside any lambda ---
(:: mkPlain (-> a b (Two a b)))

(fn (mkPlain x y) (Mk x y))

; --- 3: field 0 is the lambda's argument, field 1 a capture ---
(:: mkLam1 (-> String String (Two String String)))

(fn (mkLam1 s t) ((lambda (x) (Mk x t)) s))

; --- 4: both fields lambda arguments, at depths 1 and 0 ---
(:: mkLam2 (-> String String (Two String String)))

(fn (mkLam2 s t) (((lambda (x) (lambda (y) (Mk x y))) s) t))

; --- 5: the same lambda shape over a word payload ---
(:: viaLamInt (-> Int (Option Int)))

(fn (viaLamInt n) ((lambda (x) (Some x)) n))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  {
    ; --- 1, 2: outside a lambda, then inside one ---
    (let ((a (strConcat "ab" "cd")))
      (let ((p (cast Int (wrap a))))
        {
          (println (shapeOf p))
          (println (payloadRc p))
        }
      )
    )
    (let ((b (strConcat "ab" "cd")))
      (let ((p (cast Int (viaLam b))))
        {
          (println (shapeOf p))
          (println (payloadRc p))
        }
      )
    )
    ; --- 3: two reference fields, plain then one lambda deep ---
    (let ((c (strConcat "ef" "gh")))
      (let ((d (strConcat "ij" "kl")))
        {
          (println (shapeOf
            (cast Int (mkPlain c d))
          ))
          (println (shapeOf
            (cast Int (mkLam1 c d))
          ))
          ; --- 4: two lambdas deep, both fields lambda arguments ---
          (println (shapeOf
            (cast Int (mkLam2 c d))
          ))
        }
      )
    )
    ; --- 5: a word payload through the same lambda stays LEAF ---
    (println (shapeOf
      (cast Int (viaLamInt 7))
    ))
    0
  }
)
